                                                        <script>
                                                            const faqData = {
                                                                general: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is an Adaptive AI Development Company?",
                                                                        a: "An Adaptive AI Development Company builds AI systems that continuously update their own behavior, predictions, and decisions based on new data and feedback. The adaptive system manages its own performance in production."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is the difference between adaptive AI and standard AI?",
                                                                        a: "Standard AI models are trained once and deployed as fixed systems, as their parameters do not change in production. Adaptive AI updates its parameters from production data, environmental feedback, or user interactions continuously."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "When does a business need adaptive AI rather than a standard static model?",
                                                                        a: "Adaptive AI is the right architecture when the data distribution changes faster than periodic retraining can track, the feedback signal for correct model behavior is available in real time in production, or the deployment environment is too dynamic and unpredictable for a static model."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What are the main types of adaptive AI systems?",
                                                                        a: "The main types of Adaptive AI Development Solutions are online machine learning, continual learning, reinforcement learning, active learning, and contextual bandits for real-time exploration-exploitation optimization."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What industries benefit most from adaptive AI development?",
                                                                        a: "Financial services, retail and e-commerce, healthcare, manufacturing, media, and autonomous systems, as any industry where data distributions shift continuously and model decay creates measurable cost."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does adaptive AI handle the risk of learning the wrong thing from bad data?",
                                                                        a: "Our adaptive systems include data quality validation before every update, anomaly detection on incoming feedback signals, performance guardrails that block updates degrading monitored metrics below defined thresholds, and automatic rollback to the prior model version."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is catastrophic forgetting and how does continual learning prevent it?",
                                                                        a: "Catastrophic forgetting is the tendency of a neural network to lose performance on previously learned tasks when trained on new ones, as new learning overwrites the parameters encoding prior knowledge. Continual learning prevents this through elastic weight consolidation and progressive network architectures."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Is adaptive AI more expensive to build than a standard AI system?",
                                                                        a: "Adaptive AI Development requires additional engineering for drift detection, online update pipelines, feedback collection, safety boundaries, and audit infrastructure are typically 30-50% more initial investment than a comparable static system. The return on that investment comes from eliminating the quarterly retraining cycle cost and the accuracy degradation between cycles."
                                                                    }
                                                                ],

                                                                business: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is reinforcement learning and how is it different from supervised learning?",
                                                                        a: "Supervised learning trains a model on a labeled dataset where the correct answer is provided for every training example. Reinforcement learning trains an agent through trial and error as the agent takes actions, receives reward or penalty signals from the environment, and optimizes its policy to maximize cumulative reward over time."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does online machine learning work in production?",
                                                                        a: "Adaptive Machine Learning Development Services for online learning build systems where the model receives each new data point as it arrives, computes an incremental gradient update from that single example, and updates its parameters before processing the next data point rather than accumulating thousands of examples into a batch and running a full training cycle. "
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is concept drift and how does your drift detection work?",
                                                                        a: "Concept drift is the phenomenon where the statistical relationship between input features and the target variable changes over time; for example, the correlation between a user's browsing behavior and their purchase intent changes as preferences evolve. Our drift detection uses statistical tests to compare incoming production data distributions against the training baseline."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does your active learning system decide which data points to label?",
                                                                        a: "Our active learning query strategy evaluates the model's uncertainty for each candidate unlabeled data point by selecting the points where the model is least confident, where multiple models disagree most, or where the expected information gain is highest. These high-value points are routed to the labeling queue, making each labeling investment more informative than random sampling."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can an adaptive AI system be deployed in a privacy-regulated environment?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. Our Adaptive AI Development Solutions include federated learning architectures where model updates are computed locally on data that never leaves the source system, with only gradient updates aggregated centrally. Differential privacy noise addition further protects against inference attacks on the aggregated updates by enabling adaptive learning in GDPR, HIPAA, and CCPA-regulated environments."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How do you ensure a reinforcement learning agent doesn't take harmful actions in production?",
                                                                        a: "We define explicit action space constraints before deployment by configuring the boundaries within which the RL agent can make autonomous decisions, the conditions that trigger a safe fallback to a conservative default policy, and the human override protocol that pauses autonomous operation when boundary conditions are detected."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is the difference between fine-tuning and continual learning?",
                                                                        a: "Fine-tuning takes a pre-trained model and trains it further on new data, but this typically causes catastrophic forgetting, where performance on the original training domain degrades as the new domain data updates the same parameters. Continual learning uses architectural techniques to integrate new domain knowledge while actively protecting the parameters that encode prior domain performance."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How long does it take for an adaptive AI system to show improvement over the baseline?",
                                                                        a: "Timeline depends on the update frequency and feedback volume. Online learning systems processing thousands of transactions daily can show measurable accuracy improvement within days of deployment. RL pricing agents typically show measurable revenue lift within 2-4 weeks as the policy accumulates sufficient experience."
                                                                    }
                                                                ],
                                                                pricing: [
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How do we measure the ROI of an adaptive AI system?",
                                                                        a: "The primary ROI metrics are accuracy maintained over time, retraining cycle cost avoided, business metric improvement attributable to accuracy improvement as fraud losses prevented, revenue from personalization lift, and data science team capacity freed from maintenance for new capability development."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What governance does an adaptive AI system require?",
                                                                        a: "Adaptive AI governance requires an audit trail documenting every update, performance monitoring with defined acceptable ranges, bias monitoring confirming fairness metrics are maintained through updates, human oversight checkpoints for high-risk update decisions, safe fallback and rollback capability, and, for regulated industries."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How do we handle regulatory examination of an adaptive AI system?",
                                                                        a: "Our Adaptive Artificial Intelligence Development practice delivers a governance package with every system as an audit trail of every model update, performance benchmark comparison, data provenance records, bias monitoring reports, safety boundary documentation, and human override event log. This package is designed to satisfy the documentation requirements of SR 11-7 model risk management examinations, EU AI Act conformity assessments, and sector-specific regulatory review."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "Can an adaptive AI system be deployed on-premises or in a private cloud?",
                                                                        a: "Yes. All adaptive AI system components, such as the online learning pipeline, drift detection, feedback collection, model serving, and monitoring, can be deployed entirely within your private cloud VPC or on-premises. For environments requiring federated learning, local nodes update independently, and only gradient aggregates cross network boundaries."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What happens if an adaptive system learns something harmful from adversarial inputs?",
                                                                        a: "Our adaptive systems include input validation filtering adversarial signals before they enter the learning pipeline, statistical anomaly detection on feedback distributions flagging unusual learning signals, performance guardrails blocking updates that degrade monitored metrics below thresholds, and human review gates for high-stakes update decisions."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How do we communicate adaptive AI decisions to end users and stakeholders?",
                                                                        a: "Our explainability integration computes SHAP value attributions for every adaptive model output are showing which features drove the current prediction and their relative importance, even as model parameters evolve through adaptive updates. For RL agents, policy visualization shows the action-value function driving each decision. Stakeholder dashboards translate these technical signals into business-readable performance metrics."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "What is the minimum data volume required for adaptive AI to be effective?",
                                                                        a: "Data volume requirements vary significantly by adaptive architecture. Contextual bandits require fewer than 1,000 examples to produce meaningful initial estimates, with improvement from every subsequent interaction. Online learning for structured data classification can produce useful models from hundreds of examples."
                                                                    },
                                                                    {
                                                                        q: "How does Clarisco ensure an adaptive AI system continues to improve rather than stagnate?",
                                                                        a: "Long-run adaptive system improvement is maintained through: exploration rate scheduling, ensuring the system continues to seek new information rather than exploiting existing knowledge exclusively; periodic architecture review evaluating whether the adaptive mechanism remains appropriate as the system matures; feedback pipeline quality monitoring detecting degradation in the signal quality driving updates; and capability extension engagements."
                                                                    }
                                                                ]
                                                            };

                                                            function createFaq(section, id) {
                                                                const container = document.getElementById(id);
                                                                faqData[section].forEach((item, index) => {
                                                                    const html = `<div class="accordion-item">
                                                                        <p class="accordion-header">
                                                                        <button class="accordion-button ${index !== 0 ? 'collapsed' : ''}" 
                                                                        data-bs-toggle="collapse" 
                                                                        data-bs-target="#${section}${index}">
                                                                        <span class="faq-icon"><i class="bi bi-book"></i></span>
                                                                        <span class="faq-title">${item.q}</span>
                                                                        </button>
                                                                        </p>
                                                                        <div id="${section}${index}" class="accordion-collapse collapse ${index === 0 ? 'show' : ''}"  data-bs-parent="#${id}">
                                                                        <div class="accordion-body">${item.a}</div>
                                                                        </div>
                                                                        </div>`;
                                                                    container.insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend", html);
                                                                });
                                                            }
                                                            createFaq("general", "generalFaq");
                                                            createFaq("business", "businessFaq");
                                                            createFaq("pricing", "pricingFaq");
                                                        </script>

                                                        <script>
                                                            $(document).ready(function ($) {
                                                                //Check if an element was in a screen
                                                                function isScrolledIntoView(elem) {
                                                                    var docViewTop = $(window).scrollTop();
                                                                    var docViewBottom = docViewTop + $(window).height();
                                                                    var elemTop = $(elem).offset().top;
                                                                    var elemBottom = elemTop + $(elem).height();
                                                                    return ((elemBottom <= docViewBottom));
                                                                }
                                                                //Count up code
                                                                function countUp() {
                                                                    $('.counter').each(function () {
                                                                        var $this = $(this), // <- Don't touch this variable. It's pure magic.
                                                                            countTo = $this.attr('data-count');
                                                                        ended = $this.attr('ended');

                                                                        if (ended != "true" && isScrolledIntoView($this)) {
                                                                            $({ countNum: $this.text() }).animate({
                                                                                countNum: countTo
                                                                            },
                                                                                {
                                                                                    duration: 2500, //duration of counting
                                                                                    easing: 'swing',
                                                                                    step: function () {
                                                                                        $this.text(Math.floor(this.countNum));
                                                                                    },
                                                                                    complete: function () {
                                                                                        $this.text(this.countNum);
                                                                                    }
                                                                                });
                                                                            $this.attr('ended', 'true');
                                                                        }
                                                                    });
                                                                }
                                                                //Start animation on page-load
                                                                if (isScrolledIntoView(".counter")) {
                                                                    countUp();
                                                                }
                                                                //Start animation on screen
                                                                $(document).scroll(function () {
                                                                    if (isScrolledIntoView(".counter")) {
                                                                        countUp();
                                                                    }
                                                                });
                                                            });
                                                        </script>

